 "response": "Tepi's budget is now **$2246K**.\n\n**Method.** I ignored every message not from the Finance Office, since only Finance can change the budget. Then I worked out which Finance withdrawals still count. A withdrawal only targets an earlier update, so I went from the last record back to the first. A withdrawal counts only if no later, still-valid withdrawal cancels it.\n\n**Notable withdrawal chains.**\n- #0002 stays cancelled. The chain runs #1545 \u2192 #0504 \u2192 #0031 \u2192 #0018 \u2192 #0005 \u2192 #0002, and #1545, #0031 and #0005 are the ones in force.\n- #0035 is back in force. #0920 cancels #0331, which brings back #0176. That cancels #0119, bringing back #0110, which cancels #0084, bringing back #0078. #0078 then cancels #0069, so #0035 applies again.\n- #0260 stays cancelled. #1593 cancels #1396, so #0987 stands and #0260 remains withdrawn.\n\n**Result.** Starting from #0001 ($1810K), I applied every remaining Finance increase and decrease in record order. That leaves 113 budget updates excluded as withdrawn. The final change is #1596 (a decrease of $15K), which brings the running total to $2246K.\n\nThis rests on one long hand-kept running total, so a single slip would change the figure.\n\nANSWER: $2246K",
